<italic>&#x000f8;</italic> , and observing diplotype [12][12] is 1- <italic>&#x000f8;</italic> .</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2.</label><caption><p>The Type I Error Estimated from 1000 Simulation Replicates Under the 2 and 3-SNP Models with Nominal Level 0.05</p></caption><table frame="border" rules="all" width="100%"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">n</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">2-SNP model</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">3-SNP Model</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">100</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.073</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.06</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">200</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.056</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.055</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">300</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.058</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.054</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">400</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.045</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.049</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">500</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.047</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.048</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3.</label><caption><p>The Mean MLEs with their Square Root Mean Square Errors (RMSEs) (in Parentheses) of Population and Quantitative Parameters of the BTNs Estimated from 1000 Simulation Replicates Under the 2-SNP Model</p></caption><table frame="border" rules="all" width="100%"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>n</italic></th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>0</sub> = 0.5</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>1</sub> = 1</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>2</su